index=entra sourcetype="azure:loganalytics:securityevent" (EventID=4624 OR EventID=4625) earliest=-1h latest=now
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` Detection (SPL): RDP / interactive (or internet network) logon on DC01    ```
```                  from an IP outside the operator allowlist                 ```
``` Lab:             Contoso Health Identity Platform - Splunk second SIEM     ```
``` KQL twin:        lab/kql/dc-logon-outside-operator-allowlist.kql           ```
``` -------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` STAND-IN: Splunk Enterprise 60-day TRIAL over logs REPLAYED from Log       ```
``` Analytics. NEEDS the replay to carry SecurityEvent (ingest-from-           ```
``` loganalytics.sh -T ... SecurityEvent) and the contoso_operator_ips lookup  ```
``` (transforms.conf [contoso_operator_ips], match_type CIDR(IpRange), file  ```
``` contoso_operator_ips.csv: IpRange,Owner,ExpiresOn). The CSV holds the     ```
``` sensitive operator IP: it is gitignored, splunk-up.sh creates it header-  ```
``` only (mode 0600) when missing, and the operator fills it with the SAME    ```
``` /32 rows as Terraform operator_ip_ranges (the Sentinel watchlist          ```
``` operator_ips is Terraform-owned). An empty lookup = every source alerts  ```
``` (AllowlistLoaded false), never silence.                                  ```
```                                                                            ```
``` WHAT IT CATCHES                                                             ```
```   ADR 0013: DC01 has a public IP with RDP and LDAPS open to the operator  ```
```   allowlist only. 4624/4625 on DC01 whose source is not an unexpired      ```
```   allowlist entry: LogonType 10/7 (RDP) from anywhere, LogonType 3 or 8   ```
```   (NetworkCleartext: LDAP simple bind; verify which type an LDAPS simple  ```
```   bind logs) from a public address. Severity column: High = a successful ```
```   logon, Medium = failures only (the port answered someone it should not: ```
```   NSG drift).                                                             ```
```   AllowlistLoaded = false: the lookup was empty, so every source alerts.  ```
``` MITRE ATT&CK: T1133 External Remote Services; T1021.001 RDP; T1078.002.   ```
```                                                                            ```
``` KQL -> SPL TRANSLATION                                                      ```
```   trim_start(::ffff:, IpAddress)       -> replace(IpAddress, ^::ffff:, )   ```
```   parse_ipv4() not null                -> dotted-quad match()              ```
```   ipv4_is_private()                    -> cidrmatch on the RFC 1918 ranges ```
```   _GetWatchlist(operator_ips) + ipv4_is_in_any_range                       ```
```                                        -> lookup contoso_operator_ips (CIDR ```
```                                           match on IpRange, max_matches 10), ```
```                                           then only entries whose          ```
```                                           ExpiresOn (yyyy-mm-dd) is still  ```
```                                           in the future count              ```
```   toscalar(make_set) for AllowlistLoaded -> eval subsearch over           ```
```                                           inputlookup, returning a count   ```
```   endswith $ (machine accounts)        -> match() with [$]$               ```
```   summarize ... by Account, Domain, Host, Computer, SourceIp               ```
```                                        -> stats BY the same; null domain   ```
```                                           or computer filled with (none)   ```
```                                           first (stats drops null keys)    ```
```                                                                            ```
``` SCHEDULE: PT5M / PT1H, base severity High (Severity column = dynamic),     ```
``` throttled 1 h per Account + SourceIp.                                       ```
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` @stanza Contoso - DC01 logon from outside the operator allowlist ```
``` @conf description = RDP or interactive logon on DC01, or a network logon from a public IP, whose source is not on the operator_ips allowlist (ADR 0013). High on success. KQL twin: lab/kql/dc-logon-outside-operator-allowlist.kql ```
``` @conf disabled = 0 ```
``` @conf enableSched = 1 ```
``` @conf cron_schedule = */5 * * * * ```
``` @conf dispatch.earliest_time = -1h ```
``` @conf dispatch.latest_time = now ```
``` @conf counttype = number of events ```
``` @conf relation = greater than ```
``` @conf quantity = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.track = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.severity = 5 ```
``` @conf alert.expires = 7d ```
``` @conf alert.digest_mode = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.fields = Account,SourceIp ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.period = 1h ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_app = search ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_view = search ```
| where in(EventID, 4624, 4625) AND in(LogonType, 10, 7, 3, 8)
| eval Host=upper(mvindex(split(coalesce(Computer, ""), "."), 0))
| where in(Host, "DC01")
| eval SourceIp=replace(coalesce(IpAddress, ""), "^::ffff:", "")
| where SourceIp!="" AND NOT in(SourceIp, "-", "127.0.0.1", "::1")
| eval IsIpv4=if(match(SourceIp, "^[0-9]{1,3}([.][0-9]{1,3}){3}$"), "true", "false")
| eval IsPrivate=if(IsIpv4=="true" AND (cidrmatch("10.0.0.0/8", SourceIp) OR cidrmatch("172.16.0.0/12", SourceIp) OR cidrmatch("192.168.0.0/16", SourceIp)), "true", "false")
| lookup contoso_operator_ips IpRange AS SourceIp OUTPUT IpRange AS MatchedRange ExpiresOn
| eval LiveExpiry=mvfilter(strptime(ExpiresOn, "%Y-%m-%d") > now())
| eval Allowlisted=if(IsIpv4=="true" AND coalesce(mvcount(LiveExpiry), 0) > 0, "true", "false")
| where Allowlisted=="false"
| where in(LogonType, 10, 7) OR IsPrivate=="false"
| where NOT match(coalesce(TargetUserName, ""), "[$]$")
| eval Kind=case(EventID==4624 AND LogonType==10, "RDP logon", EventID==4624 AND LogonType==7, "RDP reconnect / unlock", EventID==4624 AND LogonType==8, "Cleartext (LDAP simple) bind from a public IP", EventID==4624, "Network logon from a public IP (NLA or LDAPS bind)", in(LogonType, 10, 7), "Failed RDP logon", LogonType==8, "Failed cleartext (LDAP simple) bind from a public IP", true(), "Failed network logon from a public IP")
| eval Account=lower(TargetUserName), IsSuccess=if(EventID==4624, 1, 0), IsFailure=if(EventID==4625, 1, 0)
| fillnull value="(none)" TargetDomainName Computer
| stats max(_time) AS LastEpoch, min(_time) AS FirstEpoch, count AS Events, sum(IsSuccess) AS Successes, sum(IsFailure) AS Failures, values(Kind) AS Kinds, values(LogonType) AS LogonTypes, values(WorkstationName) AS Workstations, first(TargetUserSid) AS AccountSid, first(IsPrivate) AS IsPrivate BY Account TargetDomainName Host Computer SourceIp
| rename TargetDomainName AS AccountDomain
| eval AccountDomain=if(AccountDomain=="(none)", "", AccountDomain), Computer=if(Computer=="(none)", "", Computer)
| eval Kinds=mvindex(Kinds, 0, 4), LogonTypes=mvindex(LogonTypes, 0, 3), Workstations=mvindex(Workstations, 0, 4)
| eval AllowlistEntries=[| inputlookup contoso_operator_ips | where strptime(ExpiresOn, "%Y-%m-%d") > now() | stats count AS n | return $n]
| eval AllowlistLoaded=if(AllowlistEntries > 0, "true", "false")
| eval Tier0Account=if(match(Account, "^(tier0-admin-[0-9]{2}|administrator)$"), "true", "false")
| eval Verdict=case(Successes > 0 AND IsPrivate=="true", "Logon on DC01 from inside the VNet - no jump host exists, treat as lateral movement", Successes > 0, "DC01 accepted a logon from a public IP outside the operator allowlist", true(), "Failed logons from outside the allowlist - the port is reachable: check the NSG")
| eval Verdict=if(AllowlistLoaded=="true", Verdict, Verdict . " (operator_ips watchlist empty or missing: every source alerts)")
| eval Severity=if(Successes > 0, "High", "Medium")
| eval _time=LastEpoch
| eval TimeGenerated=strftime(LastEpoch, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%3N%z"), FirstSeen=strftime(FirstEpoch, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%3N%z")
| sort 0 - _time
| table TimeGenerated, Severity, Verdict, Account, AccountDomain, AccountSid, Tier0Account, Host, Computer, SourceIp, IsPrivate, Successes, Failures, Events, Kinds, LogonTypes, Workstations, FirstSeen, AllowlistLoaded
